ital expenditure efficiency\n\n**Free Cash Flow Projections:**\n- 2026E: $108B\n- 2027E: $118B  \n- 2028E: $128B\n- Terminal growth rate: 2.5%\n\n### Discount Rate Calculation\n\n**Weighted Average Cost of Capital (WACC): 8.2%**\n\nComponents:\n- Risk-free rate: 4.1% (10-year Treasury)\n- Market risk premium: 6.0%\n- Beta coefficient: 1.15\n- Cost of equity: 11.0%\n- After-tax cost of debt: 3.2%\n- Debt-to-equity ratio: 15%\n\n**DCF Valuation Result: $255 per share**\n\n## Peer Comparison Analysis\n\n### Technology Peer Group\n\n**Primary Comparables:**\n- Microsoft (MSFT): 32.1x forward P/E\n- Alphabet (GOOGL): 24.8x forward P/E\n- Meta (META): 22.5x forward P/E\n- Amazon (AMZN): 35.2x forward P/E\n\n**AAPL Premium Justification:**\nApple commands a premium valuation due to:\n- Superior gross margins (46% vs. peer average 38%)\n- Ecosystem lock-in effects\n- Brand strength and pricing power\n- Capital allocation excellence\n- Consistent cash flow generation\n\n**Peer-Adjusted Valuation:**\n- Median peer multiple: 28.7x\n- AAPL quality premium: 5-8%\n- Justified forward P/E: 30.2x\n- **Target Price: $250 per share**\n\n### Hardware Peer Analysis\n\n**Consumer Electronics Comparables:**\n- Samsung Electronics: 12.5x P/E\n- Sony Corporation: 15.8x P/E\n- Nintendo: 18.2x P/E\n\nApple's premium to hardware peers reflects:\n- Software/services integration\n- Higher-margin business model\n- Superior brand positioning\n- Ecosystem monetization\n\n## Scenario Analysis\n\n### Bull Case Scenario (+25% upside)\n**Target Price: $315**\n\nKey drivers:\n- Services revenue acceleration (18% CAGR)\n- Successful AR/VR product launch\n- Market share gains in emerging markets\n- Margin expansion to 50%+\n\n### Base Case Scenario (Current target)\n**Target Price: $255**\n\nAssumptions:\n- Steady iPhone replacement cycles\n- Services growth at 13% CAGR\n- Margin stability around 47%\n- Continued capital returns\n\n### Bear Case Scenario (-15% downside)\n**Target Price: $210**\n\nRisk factors:\n- iPhone demand deterioration\n- Regulatory pressure on App Store\n- Increased competition in services\n- Margin compression\n\n## Valuation Sensitivity Analysis\n\n**Key Variables Impact on Fair Value:**\n\n| Variable | -10% | -5% | Base | +5% | +10% |\n|----------|------|-----|------|-----|------|\n| Revenue Growth | $230 | $242 | $255 | $268 | $282 |\n| WACC | $285 | $268 | $255 | $243 | $232 |\n| Terminal Growth | $240 | $247 | $255 | $264 | $274 |\n| Margins | $235 | $245 | $255 | $265 | $275 |\n\n## Asset-Based Valuation\n\n**Balance Sheet Analysis:**\n- Cash and equivalents: $162B\n- Total assets: $385B\n- Intangible assets: $45B\n- Net asset value per share: $240\n\n**Liquidation Value Considerations:**\n- Brand value: $80-100B\n- IP portfolio: $25-35B\n- Real estate: $15-20B\n- **Conservative asset value: $240 per share**\n\n## Dividend and Capital Returns Analysis\n\n**Capital Allocation Framework:**\n- Dividend yield: 0.5% (sustainable and growing)\n- Share buyback program: $90B annually\n- Total shareholder returns: 4-6% annually\n- Dividend growth rate: 5-7% annually\n\n**Return of Capital Impact:**\n- Share count reduction: 3-4% annually\n- EPS accretion from buybacks: $0.15-0.20 per share\n- Dividend sustainability score: AAA\n\n## Valuation Risks and Considerations\n\n**Upside Risks:**\n- Faster services adoption\n- Successful new product categories\n- Market share expansion\n- Margin improvement\n\n**Downside Risks:**\n- Regulatory intervention\n- Competitive pressure\n- Economic downturn impact\n- Technology disruption\n\n## Investment Recommendation\n\n**Rating: BUY**\n**Price Target: $255 (12-month)**\n**Risk Rating: Medium**\n\n**Investment Thesis:**\nApple represents a high-quality growth company trading at reasonable valuations relative to its competitive advantages and cash generation capabilities. The company's ecosystem approach, brand strength, and capital allocation discipline support our positive investment view.\n\n**Key Catalys